  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT WED SEP 2 2026\n\nThe headline event for central Alabama's weather through the rest\nof the week will continue to be the heat. Upper level heat dome\ncentered just to our north will continue to help get air \ntemperatures well into the 90s each afternoon, with heat indices\ntopping out near or above 105 degrees. Ongoing Heat Advisory looks\ngood. One thing to watch is another tropical wave that is \nforecast to scoot westward across northern FL and along the Gulf \ncoast Thursday night into Saturday. This feature will likely bring\nhigher rain chances to our southern counties during this time\nframe, which may also allow us to trim back the Heat Advisory\narea. Will keep the status quo for now, and reevaluate the\nAdvisory if/when confidence in the rainy scenario increases.\n\nAs we head into Sunday, the center of the upper ridge heads back\nto the west, and puts us back into a north/northeast flow regime.\nThis should allow POPs to climb back up to at least climo levels,\nand also temper the heat a bit into early next week. However, the\nmodels are coming into agreement that the upper ridge will shift\nback eastward in the Tuesday/Wednesday time frame, suggesting that\nthe excessive heat may not quite be over for us.\n\n/61/",
